":null,"provenance":{"dataset":"NASA POWER (MERRA-2) · TO3","version":"POWER Version 10.0.0","doi":null,"landing_page":"https://power.larc.nasa.gov/","accessed":"2026-11-14","processing":["read the whole globe for the variable from the temporal (location-chunked) store, in latitude bands covering the full time axis","masked fill value -999.0","country value = mean of the 2° map squares that overlap the country, weighted by the overlapping area (mainland and islands within about 1,000 km)","monthly series 1981-01 to 2025-12 (complete years)","anomalies from the calendar-month normal; Sen's slope, Mann-Kendall (Yue-Wang), OLS with effective sample size (trend_stats.py)"],"synthetic":false,"caveat":"Data: MERRA-2 reanalysis, a weather model corrected by observations, about 50 km squares (averaged into 2° squares; coastal squares include some sea). The trend is a straight line through 1981–2025; it shows what changed, not why."}}